{"name":"Eden Prairie","hex":"#95863c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Eden Prairie","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in Hennepin County, Minnesota, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Eden_Prairie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eden Prairie, Minnesota","blocks":[{"text":"Eden Prairie is a city in Hennepin County, Minnesota, United States. It had a population of 64,198 at the 2020 census, making it the 16th-largest city in the state. The city is adjacent to the north bank of the Minnesota River, upstream from its confluence with the Mississippi River, about 12 miles (19 km) southwest of downtown Minneapolis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/EPCH.jpg/330px-EPCH.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eden_Prairie%2C_Minnesota","wikidata":"Q985558"},{"title":"Prairie","blocks":[{"text":"Prairies are ecosystems considered part of the temperate grasslands, savannas, and shrublands biome by ecologists, based on similar temperate climates, moderate rainfall, and a composition of grasses, herbs, and shrubs, rather than trees, as the dominant vegetation type. Temperate grassland regions include the Pampas of Argentina, Brazil, and Uruguay, and the steppe of Romania, Ukraine, Russia, and Kazakhstan. Lands typically referred to as \"prairie\" tend to be in North America. The term encompasses the lower and mid-latitude of the area referred to as the Interior Plains of Canada, the United States, and Mexico. It includes all of the Great Plains as well as the wetter, hillier land to the east. From west to east, generally the drier expanse of shortgrass prairie gives way to mixed grass prairie and ultimately the richer and wetter soils of the tallgrass prairie."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/James_Woodworth_Prairie.jpg/330px-James_Woodworth_Prairie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prairie","wikidata":"Q194281"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/J.R._Cummins_Cabin.jpg/250px-J.R._Cummins_Cabin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7e/J.R._Cummins_Cabin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/J.R._Cummins_Cabin.jpg/250px-J.R._Cummins_Cabin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cummins Cabin, pre-1860","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJ.R._Cummins_Cabin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Cummins_House_6.jpg/500px-Cummins_House_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Cummins_House_6.jpg/1280px-Cummins_House_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Cummins_House_6.jpg/500px-Cummins_House_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Current photo of the Cummins-Phipps-Grill House","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACummins_House_6.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Flailing_Out_Beans_at_Cummins_Farm.jpeg/500px-Flailing_Out_Beans_at_Cummins_Farm.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Flailing_Out_Beans_at_Cummins_Farm.jpeg/500px-Flailing_Out_Beans_at_Cummins_Farm.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flailing out beans at Cummins Farm","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlailing_Out_Beans